# Unity is the game now

Until the user says otherwise, **Vacancy lives in `Unity/`**. Do not update the browser prototype.

## Do not touch

- `js/`
- `index.html`
- `css/`
- any other web-prototype files

Even when a task would be “the same change in JS and Unity,” make it **only in Unity**.

## Do

- Implement layout, story, HUD, pathing, arrivals, and playable behavior in `Unity/Assets/`
- Keep Project RM (`hotel-simulator`) out of this repo; do not copy RM C#

## Exception

Edit the JS prototype only if the user explicitly asks to update it.
